der and, once compaction acts, removes the entries themselves.\\\"],\n \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"The drift was exercised for three rounds by construction; no bound on rounds or counter values, and no automatic repair inside the sealed configuration, was established.\\\",\n  \\\"Loss-triggered and timer-triggered re-synchronization were not exercised; the producers observed are explicit reconnected() calls and ordinary leader changes with one node cut off.\\\",\n  \\\"Only three-node clusters were used, with in-memory storage, no persistence across restarts and one snapshot-capable entry type; the compaction witnesses depend on that entry type's snapshot semantics.\\\",\n  \\\"Several comparisons in the repeated-rounds, trim and snapshot receipts came out unknown because their admissions shared event names across cases in one execution; those states are asserted from the sampled operands, with the violated comparisons cited above.\\\",\n  \\\"The consequence set stays within index accounting, readability and compaction; the sealed configuration admits no further entries, so no value is mis-assigned.\\\"],\n \\\"joint_history\\\":(\\\"Eight receipts of one harness lineage, each read on its own samples and never combined arithmetically: 8b314551f1e049fcbf73a358f8ddf2c8 (resync, control), 9125b6a531234e7d9d2fa8cbb817df63 (single resync, read of index 6), 6cdcff36336646859bffb9e8c3e39789 (newterm), dda5bb4179154e3abe90e69f5267b3ea (staleleader), fd0b8be59c8f466fbf7768abb08f93b5 (snapshot-capable resync), 6c879304cdde4ddd8e1640207cdbf94d (three reconnection rounds), ec3329dc273e452aa92bcd44652c116a (drift then trim) and e70b8baa087246c78ea3a64f24b8e97c (drift then snapshot). Each successor reproduces the earlier witnesses and adds one case.\\\"),\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"27bf7fc0875c4342966bd3dc15df80ec-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":5,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"sync_log adds the carried StopSign on top of sync_idx plus the suffix, and each further re-synchronization adds another index\\\"},\n  {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"3ed5ddd94bce4e94a2dc5b7bb417c18a-knowledge-1\\\",\\\"revision\\\":5,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"the decided-log read loses the entries after such a re-synchronization\\\"},\n  {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"e40cd046de9e4f37b5761260b8dc599e-knowledge-1\\\",\\\"revision\\\":4,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"the condition is the resume point covering the StopSign's index\\\"},\n  {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"e40cd046de9e4f37b5761260b8dc599e-knowledge-2\\\",\\\"revision\\\":2,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"the leader decides the reported accepted index without bounding it to its own log\\\"},\n  {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"fa5a6edbbfe243c7a66eb9f3eed7433b-knowledge-1\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"a candidate leader syncing from a follower is inflated in its own accepted index\\\"},\n  {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"e65d63f4057d4c5bbe8390ac06b30fce-knowledge-2\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"the recorded accepted and decided indexes drift one index per re-synchronization round\\\"},\n  {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"4c57d4fe287e4534a689e56689def6a8-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"trim accepted a drifted bound and compacted past the content the leader held\\\"},\n  {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"856d6fe2b3a14c7ab6dbed00026ba199-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"the snapshot path accepted a drifted bound and produced a snapshot holding none of the entries\\\"}]}\nup={\\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Consolidate the parent account so it carries all four witnessed consequence classes, including the two compaction ones that until now lived only in the child accounts. The rewrite names the cause once, cites each class with its receipt and decisive events (per-replica index inflation and lost reconfiguration endpoint; the one-index-per-round drift; the leader's decision at a drifted index; and the two compaction paths, where trim compacted 7 for six indices of content and snapshot(Some(8), false) produced a snapshot holding none of the five decided entries), keeps the same-run controls and the counterevidence that bounds each class, and lists the child knowledge entries it relies on so the linkage is recorded rather than implied.\\\"),\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[interp]}\njson.dump(up, open('update.json','w'), indent=1); print('written')\nPY\ntimeout 120 /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_09-22-17-omnipaxos-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -c 700\"","aggregated_output":"written\n{\"valid\": false, \"run_id\": \"d99e3b9fb63f4d89b4e0c59b4352dd5b\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 2217.289469602001, \"diagnostics\": [{\"details\": {}, \"code\": \"submission\", \"category\": \"semantic\", \"task\": \"\", \"candidate_version\": 0, \"object_ids\": [], \"paths\": [], \"material_ids\": [], \"message\": \"Interpretation must identify its investigation and fixed experiment\", \"allowed\": []}], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
